1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/175237698/orrie-everett-gilbertson
2 CONT
2 CONT Orrie Everett Gilbertson was born on May 8, 1924, near Downer, Minnesota of Clay County, the son of Gustav R. and Olga (Enger) Gilbertson.  The family was of Norwegian heritage.  He attended grade school in Tansem Township and lat
2 CONC er in Humbolt Township near Barnesville.  He also worked on area farms.  In January of 1945, he entered the US Marine Corp. and was honorably discharged in October of 1946.  On November 15, 1947, he married Arlene C. Bekkerus at t
2 CONC he Barnesville Assembly of God Church.  The couple resided and farmed near Rollag until August of 1999.  Orrie worked at the Pelican Turkey Plant for over 22 years.  The couple currently resides in Pelican Rapids.  He was a member
2 CONC  of the Barnesville Assembly of God where he served as treasurer for 40 years and Sunday school teacher for 35 years.  He also was clerk of Tansem Township for 9 years.  His hobbies include woodworking and trapping.  In June and J
2 CONC uly of 1990, Orrie and Arlene enjoyed a 3 week self-guided tour of Norway.  For Orrie’s 80th birthday, they went to Washington DC for the dedication of the World War II Memorial.  His family includes his wife Arlene, of Pelican Ra
2 CONC pids, MN; one daughter Faith (Pastor Richard) Davis of Lorton, Virginia; three sons: Daniel (Christine) of Bonners Ferry, Idaho; Joel of Fargo, ND; and Mark of Fargo; four grandchildren: Jonathon (Elisabeth); Christa (Brian) Stapl
2 CONC es; Melissa and Jesse; one sister Etta Bekkerus, of Glyndon, MN; along with numerous nieces, nephews, cousins, and a host of friends.  Preceding him in death were his parents, Gustav and Olga; his granddaughter Ruthann; one sister
2 CONC  Martha (Vern) Shaner; one brother Gordon (Claudia) Gilbertson; and a nephew Elwood Shaner. 
