1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From:  http://www.genealogybank.com/doc/obituaries/obit/127881531B7CF8D8?s_referrer=FamilySearch&utm_source=FamilySearch&s_siteloc=FSIndex&utm_medium=FSIndex&s_trackval=OT_FSrch_Index_1408_00&utm_campaign=OT_FSrch_
2 CONC Index_1408_00&fsname=
2 CONT
2 CONT Nelson, Dr. Arthur Glenn A Nelson, Dr. Arthur Glenn Arthur Glenn Nelson, M.D., died in Dallas, Tuesday, April 7, 2009, after a long and fulfilling life and career. He was 84. Born on the family farm, December 19, 1924 in Clifton, 
2 CONC Texas, Dr. Nelson graduated from UT Southwestern Medical School. His residency was at Parkland Memorial Hospital. He served his country during the Korean Conflict as a ship's surgeon in the US Navy. In the late 1950s, he was one o
2 CONC f the original founding members of Doctors Hospital in the White Rock area of Dallas. Dr. Nelson enjoyed many hobbies including photography, outdoor sports, and travel with a particular affection for Santa Fe, New Mexico and Carme
2 CONC l, California. He is preceded in death by sons Mike and Ric Nelson and grandson Mark Lanter. Dr. Nelson is survived by his loving wife Connie; children, Nancy, Mark with wife Kim, and Nita with husband Cecil; grandchildren, Leah, 
2 CONC Karen, Jessica, Luke, and Sara; great-grandchildren, Camryn and Kristin; nephew, Bryan Wilmoth with wife Cathryn and their children Emily and Anna, niece Carole with her children Tony and Chris, and nephews and nieces John Hasting
2 CONC s, Mary Ellen Hastings-Strand, Shirley Johnson, and Nellie Baldwin. Numerous other nephews and nieces and countless friends are also left to mourn his passing. A memorial service for Dr. Nelson, will be held, 4:00 PM, Monday, Apri
2 CONC l 13, 2009, Grove Hill Funeral Home Chapel.
2 CONT
