2 CONT Maren was 2 years old when her mother died after the birth of her 4th child. In 1871, Peder sold his share of the Morka farm to his brother Hans and emigrated with his new wife and 4 children.On April 15th they sailed from Christi
2 CONC ana (now Oslo) on the ship Concordia and arrived in Quebec 37 days later.The family lived in Ridgeway, Winnesheik Co., IAuntil about 1876 when they moved to Cerro Gordo Township in Lac qui Parle County, Minnesota, where Peder home
2 CONC steaded the NW quarter of section 29.While Peder built their home, the family lived in a sod house.During his early years in America, Peder used Hansen or Hanson as his surname, but sometime during the 1880's he changed his last n
2 CONC ame to Mork, an adaption of the farm Morka. Maren's father died in 1886 and is buried with his wife Lise in Borgund Lutheran Cemetary in Cerro Gordo Township, MN. Maren was employed in the home of C.W. Paige in Lac qui Parle Villa
2 CONC ge and later in the Chas. Couglin home in Dawson when she met her future husband James P. Vane.
