1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/94108675/caroline-marie-erickson
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Ole Erickson succumbs at York, Blanchardville
2 CONT
2 CONT In poor health for the past three years, Mrs. Ole Erickson, 82, town of York, died at her home in Blanchardville at 7:15 this morning. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Caroline Maria Strommen was born July 30, 1865, the daughter of Andrew and Martha Strommen, in the town of York. After her marriage to Ole Erickson, they settled in the town of York, farming until their retirement 27 years ago, wh
2 CONC en they moved to Blanchardville. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are: sons, Anton, Almon, Amos, Thomas and Andrew of Blanchardville, Edward of Woodford, and Martin of Darlington: four brothers, Anton and Melvin of Blanchardville, Frank, of Argyle, and Martin of Ironwood, MI; 11 grandc
2 CONC hildren and five great grandchildren. She was preceded in death by her husband, her parents, one brother and four sisters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be conducted Friday at 1:30 in the Saether Funeral Home and at 2 in the Blanchardville Lutheran Church, of which Mrs. Erickson was a member. Rev. T. Klevin will officiate. Burial will be in Graceland Cemetery
2 CONC , Blanchardville. Pallbearers are Maurice, Elmer, Luther, LaVon, Howard and Arthur Strommen. Times Special Services
