2 CONT
2 CONT Anton H. Emberson, 84, passed away at his farm home Thursday, March 18th, after a long illness. He had been bed-ridden for the past two years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Emberson, who had spent his entire life farming in this vicinity, was born in the town of York, Sept. 23, 1863. His parents were Hans and Carrie Loken Emberson. He was married to Carrie Lageson of Blanchardville by Rev. Paulso
2 CONC n March 22, 1895. they resided on Emberson farm one mile east of Blanchardville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are the widow, two daughters: (Alma) Mrs. Bennie Hermanson, (Clara) Mrs. Sherman Hermanson of Blanchardville; six sons, Henry and Arthur of Argyle, Bennie, Willard, Everett and Glenn of Blanchardville; three sisters, Mrs
2 CONC . Mathilda Gilbertson of Roseland, S.D., Mrs. Emma Olson of Timberland, S.D. and Mrs. Lena Hanson of Blanchardville; 13 grandchildren and one great-grandchild. He was preceded in death by his parents and one son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Sunday, March 21, at 1:30 in the Saether funeral home and at 2 in the Blanchardville Lutheran church, conducted by Rev. T. Kleven. Burial was in Graceland cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers were Wilmar Emberson, Martin Norton, Edwin Hanson, Lawrence Severson, Glenn Lageson, Donald Lageson.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased, who spent his entire lifetime in this community, was highly respected by all who knew him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Blanchardville Blade, March 25, 1948 - page 1  (Contributor JnJSchober) 
2 CONT
