2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Marie and her sister Karin came to US in 1869 with their parents.Bertha Marie told Otto Jr., "that they crossed the ocean in a sail-ship and were on the ocean for ten weeks.Enroute they encountered such a bad storm that the
2 CONC  ship sprung a leak and they had to "man the pumps'."In the latter part of June they landed at Quebec and set out for the west immediately. They crossed the Mississippi River at Prairie du Chien after the river froze over and even
2 CONC tually stopped near Clermont, Iowa (Clayton County) and began farming.This is where their mother died and was buried.Not long after her death, Hans took the girls and went on to Lyon County, Iowa, where Bertha Marie met Ole Helger
2 CONC son.They were married in Sioux City by a Presbyterian minister.Sioux City was quite a distance south.
