1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From:  https://www.genealogybank.com/doc/obituaries/obit/133ABAD76010A9F8-133ABAD76010A9F8?search_terms=roetschke
2 CONT
2 CONT Jimmie Ernest Roetschke
2 CONT
2 CONT LAKE WORTH - Jimmie Ernest Roetschke, 79, a loving husband, father, grandfather and great-grandfather, passed away Wednesday, Nov. 17, 2010. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral: 11 a.m. Saturday in Biggers Funeral Chapel. Interment: Greenwood Memorial Park. Visitation: 6 to 8 p.m. Friday at Biggers Funeral Home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jimmie was born Aug. 17, 1931, in Clifton to August and Susana Roetschke. He had resided in Lake Worth since 1960 and served on the City Council for 16 years. He retired after 34 years of service with General Motors in Arlington. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jimmy was a great provider. He was determined, gentle, softspoken, strong and giving. He loved hunting and sports. He was devoted and dedicated to his family and loved life and spending time with his family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: Wife of 52 years, Vernie Roetschke of Lake Worth; daughters, Terry O'Grady and husband, Danny, of Fort Worth and Robin Frizzell and Herman of Fort Worth; brother, Ronnie Roetschke of Midland; grandchildren, Michelle Ham
2 CONC pton, Jamie Beasley, Tyler Frizzell, Dalton Frizzell, Taylor Lauren O'Grady, and Garrett O'Grady; and great-grandchildren, Kyler Anderson, Skylar Hampton and Lily Campisi. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Biggers Funeral Home 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6100 Azle Ave., 817-237-3341 
2 CONT
2 CONT View and sign guestbook at 
2 CONT
