1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From:  http://www.genealogybank.com/doc/obituaries/obit/108C1C7A33ACC814?s_referrer=FamilySearch&utm_source=FamilySearch&s_siteloc=FSIndex&utm_medium=FSIndex&s_trackval=OT_FSrch_Index_1408_00&utm_campaign=OT_FSrch_
2 CONC Index_1408_00&fsname=
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Alton Stanley
2 CONT
2 CONT CLIFTON -- Robert Alton Stanley, 87, passed away Monday, March 7, 2005, at a Waco hospital. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral: 2 p.m. Friday at Clifton Funeral Home in Clifton with Pastor Bill Schibler officiating. Burial: Trinity Lutheran Cemetery in Clifton. Visitation: 6 to 8 p.m. Thursday at the funeral home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials: Clifton Lutheran Sunset Home, 300 S. Avenue Q, Clifton, Texas 76634, in lieu of flowers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob was born May 3, 1917, in Steiner Valley, Bosque County, across from White's Bluff on the Brazos River. He was the fourth of five children born to tenant farmers Lawrence Bernard and Fannie Katherine "Margie" Adcock Stanley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob, as his friends called him, began school in Kimball near Kopperl, attended Union Hill and graduated from Kopperl High School in 1935. In 1937, he graduated from Clifton Junior College, where he participated in football, basket
2 CONC ball and baseball. He met the love of his life, Anna Marie Seljos, while at Clifton Junior College, and they were married Dec. 23, 1938. To this union three sons were born -- Lee, Randall and Warren. Anna Marie preceded him in dea
2 CONC th in 1979. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bob taught at Harmony, Cranfills Gap and Kopperl before he was drafted into the Army on Dec. 2, 1942. He was stationed in Texas at Camp Howze and Camp Wolters and at Fort Polk, La.; Fort Belvoir, Va.; and Manila, the Philippines. 
2 CONC He was honorably discharged in January 1946. When he returned from the military, he received a bachelor's degree from North Texas in 1946 and a master of education degree from Sul Ross in 1949. In the fall of 1946, he and Anna Mar
2 CONC ie returned to Cranfills Gap, where he became a teacher, coach and principal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the fall of 1951, he went to White Settlement as the first principal at the new Brewer High School. He even wrote the school song. In 1958, he went to Granbury to be school superintendent until 1970. Later, he taught three year
2 CONC s in the Cleburne school system and was superintendent at Blum from 1973 to 1978. He retired in 1978 and devoted his time to his hobbies of fishing, hunting, gardening and raising bantam chickens. 
2 CONT
2 CONT For many years, Bob and his family were members of Trinity Lutheran Church in Fort Worth. In recent years he was a member of Ascension Lutheran Church in Cleburne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents; his wife, Anna Marie; his brother, James Calvin Stanley; and his sisters, Clara Stanley Moore, Dallas Stanley Williams and Mildred Stanley Coleman, preceded him in death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors: Sons, Lee Stanley and wife, Dorothy, of Clifton, Randall Stanley and wife, Linda, of Crowley and Warren Stanley and wife, Kathy, of Rio Vista; seven grandchildren; and two great-grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Clifton Funeral Home 
2 CONT
2 CONT Clifton, (254) 675-8611 
2 CONT
