1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From:  https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=thiele&GSfn=alice&GSmn=c.&GSbyrel=all&GSdy=2006&GSdyrel=in&GSst=46&GScntry=4&GSob=n&GRid=13989272&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice Jorgenson Thiele, 57, of Duncanville, passed away Monday, April 17, 2006 in Dallas. Funeral service will be 10 a.m. Wednesday, April 19, at Bethel Temple Church in Dallas, and a 10 a.m. service Thursday, April 20, in the Cli
2 CONC fton Funeral Home Chapel. The family will receive visitors from 6 to 7 p.m. Wednesday at the funeral home. Burial will be in the Trinity Lutheran Cemetery under the direction of Clifton Funeral Home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice was born Nov. 12, 1948, in Shreveport, La., to Alvin C. Jorgenson and Syble Faye Brandon Jorgenson. She attended Clifton Elementary, and graduated from Sinton High School in Sinton. Due to her father's employment with Hudson
2 CONC  Engineering, the family lived many different places, including La., Iowa, and Kansas.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 28, 1979, she married Larry Victor Thiele in the Trinity Lutheran Church of Clifton, and the couple had one child. She worked as an accounting clerk and was affiliated with the baptist church. Alice enjoyed arts and craft
2 CONC s, garage sale shopping, and cooking. She was a loving, caring, and devoted wife, mother and grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her father, Alvin Jorgenson.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by her husband, Larry Thiele, of Duncanville; son, Trevor Thiele, of Duncanville; grandchild, Braelyn Thiele, of Duncanville; mother, Faye Jorgenson, of Clifton; and mother-in-law, Doris Thiele, of Clifton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers will be Charles Jorgenson, Jonathan Jorgenson, J.W. Thiele, Goerge Larson, Edward Ludwig, Clarence Fields, and Kenneth Lowrance.
2 CONT
