1 NAME James Peter /Christensen/
2 GIVN James Peter
2 SURN Christensen
2 _MARNM Vane
2 NICK Jens Peter
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 2 SEP 1862
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lendum
3 STAE Hjørring
3 CTRY Danmark
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 MAR 1949
2 ADDR
3 STAE Minnesota
3 CTRY United States of America
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=15730929
2 CONT
2 CONT On September 2 1862, Jens Peter Christiansen and his twin brother, Christian Carl, were born to Christine Jensdatter and her 3rd husband, Niels Christian Christensen.Jens and Christian were born in Lendum Parish on the farm Kobber
2 CONC mark, which is only a few miles from the the farm Vaen where their father was born and the farm Norre Foldsted where their mother was born.Lendum Parish is in the Vendsyssel area of Denmark which was at that time part of Hjorring 
2 CONC Co., but now is part of Alborg County. Christine Jensdatter's first husband, Christen Christian Nielsen, died of Tuberculosis at age 28.After the death of her secnd husband Peter Larsen, Christine married Niels Christian Christens
2 CONC en who was 11 years younger.Christine and Niels separated shortly after the birth of their twin boys.When Jens and Christian were confirmed on October 1st, 1876 in Hormestead Parish, their father was listed as husmand (owner of a 
2 CONC house with a little land) in Hormestead.Very little is known about Niels, but family stories say that he was a sailor and that he had run off with a young woman.Jens told his children that as a boy he worked in a bakery.He also sa
2 CONC id that his mother would send him and his brothers and sisters into the woods to hide whenever the German soldiers came by their home. In 1879 at the age of 17, Jens Peter and his brother emigrated with his half-sister Anne Lucine
2 CONC  and her husband Julius Jensen.They settled in Sundown Township, near Springfield MN, where their mother's sister, Kirsten Jensdatter, and her children had settled earlier.After entering the US, Jens and Christian adopted the surn
2 CONC ame Vaen after the birthplace of their father.Later they changed the spelling to Vane and Jens became known as James. Sometime later James' mother Christine and his other two half-sisters immigrated and settled n Sundown Township.
2 CONC His half-sister Christine married William Christensen and lived in Pennock, MN, while his half-sister Caroline married William Heir and lived in Raymond, MN.Christ Vane, James' twin brother, maried the widow Anna Jorgensen Hemming
2 CONC sen and lived in the Sundown-Springfield area.James' mother died on January 3, 1890 at age 66 and is buried in Sundown Lutheran Cemetary where her tombstone lists her as Christine Jensen. As a young man, James worked as a laborer 
2 CONC on farms in Sundown Township.Later he worked for the Minneapolis and St. Louis Railroad as a grading contractor.In 1884, James built the bed for the first railroad to come into Dawson, MN.He remained in Dawson and established a ho
2 CONC use moving and construction company.One of his first business ventures was to dig the first city well behind the hotel.It was while digging this well that he met Maren Mork who was employed as a waitress at the hotel.
