1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=89361402  
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice Nelson
2 CONT
2 CONT admin's picture
2 CONT
2 CONT Submitted by admin on Wed, 12/03/2008 - 8:22am 
2 CONT
2 CONT assed away Wednesday, November 26, 2008, at the Palmer Lutheran Health Center in West Union. She was 93.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Monday, December 1, at the West Clermont Lutheran Church in Clermont, with the Reverend Dwight Albers officiating. Special music was provided by Marilana Sutter, organist, and Peggy Kittelson, soloist. C
2 CONC asket Bearers were Tony Conrad, Aaron Nelson, Tom Ruckdashel, John Shipton, Roger Nelson, Robert Burrett, Harold Cooney, and Ralph House. Inurnment will take place at God's Acre Cemetery, Clermont, at a later date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice Marguerite (Tatro) Nelson was born July 1, 1915, on the family farm near Clermont, to Roy Devere and Bertha Marie (Anderson) Tatro. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice was baptized and confirmed into the Lutheran Faith. She attended the Clermont schools. Alice was married to Almer Leo Nelson in the West Clermont Lutheran Church on October 25, 1934. To this union six children were born. The
2 CONC y farmed in the Clermont area. Following Almer's ill health, Alice took over the farm work for a couple of years. They then moved to Clermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice worked at Valhalla as cook and then became the Hostess there. She also worked at a café across the river in Clermont. She enjoyed doing needle work and decorating her home. Alice was a self-taught musician and liked to play 
2 CONC the piano and organ. She was also known for the lefse and other Norwegian foods that she made.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is preceded in death by her parents; her husband, Almer Leo Nelson, October 4, 1979; three sons, Robert Nelson (1982), Adrian Nelson (1976), Donald Nelson, (1942); two grandchildren; three brothers, Clarence Tatro, Orville Tat
2 CONC ro, Roy Tatro; five sisters, Viola Tann, Irene Cooney, Evelyn Tatro, Stella Tally and Andre Burrett.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice is survived by her children, Beverly (Clarence) Ruckdashel, Mesa, Ariz., Ardell Fortune, Clermont, and A. D. Nelson, Queen Creek, Ariz.; 13 grandchildren; three step-grandchildren; 32 great-grandchildren, eight great-great-g
2 CONC randchildren; and a sister, Hazel Stee, Postville.  
2 CONT
2 CONT SectionName: 
