2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  Aug. 28, 1942  Death:  Sep. 12, 1976 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adrian William Nelson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Adrian William Nelson, 34, rural Postville, were held Wednesday, Sept. 15 at 10:30 a.m. from Washington Prairie Lutheran church, rural Decorah, with the Rev. Richard Sansgaard officiating. Interment was in Pos
2 CONC tville cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died Sunday, September 12 as the result of a motorcycle accident. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born August 28, 1942 in Clayton county. His parents are Almer Leo and Alice Tatro Nelson. He was a 1960 graduate of Valley of Elgin high school and was engaged in farming. He married Sharon Gordon May 10, 1964 in Postville.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his parents, his wife, a daughter Amy, 11, and son Aaron, eight, two brothers, Robert and A. D. Nelson of Clermont, and two sisters, Mrs. Clarence (Beverly) Ruckdashel of Mesa, AZ and Mrs. Ardell Conrad of San Diego,
2 CONC  California. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of Washington Prairie church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Casket bearers were Albert Ashbacher, Darrel Crawford, David Schwinefus, William Green, Gary Larson and Jeff Feickert. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Schutte funeral home of Postville was in charge of arrangements. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Postville Herald newspaper clipping from Dorothy Schave's collection. 
2 CONT
