1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=46864456
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph L House Memorial Photos Flowers Edit Share Learn about removing the ads from this memorial... Birth: 	Jan. 17, 1932 Hawkeye Fayette County Iowa, USA Death: 	Jan. 17, 2010 Dubuque Dubuque County Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT From the January 19, 2010 edition of the Dubuque Telegraph Herald
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph L. House, 78, of Dubuque, died Sunday, Jan. 17, 2010, at his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at 10 a.m. Thursday, Jan. 21, at St. Peter Lutheran Church. Burial will be in West Union Cemetery, West Union, Iowa. Friends may call from 4 to 6 p.m. Wednesday, Jan. 20, at Hoffmann Schneider and Kitchen Funeral 
2 CONC Home, 3860 Asbury Road. Friends also may call after 9 a.m. Thursday at the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born on Jan. 17, 1932, in rural Hawkeye, Iowa, son of Fred and Mabel (Book) House. He graduated from West Union High School in 1949.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Ginny Nelson on Oct. 8, 1955, at the Little Brown Church in Nashua, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was employed by the former Northwestern Bell Telephone Co. as a lineman and later as the supply and warehouse manager. He retired in 1986, after 35 years of service.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an active member of the church and of the Northwestern Bell Pioneers of America Club, which he served as president for a period of time. He enjoyed travelling with the club across the United States. He also enjoyed the outd
2 CONC oors, camping, fishing and spending time in Clear Lake each year. After retirement, he and Ginny wintered in Port Isabelle, Texas, for 15 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT He will be remembered as a positive, warm, loving, kind, friendly person who never failed to lift up the spirits of everyone around him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are his wife of 54 years, Ginny; his children, Kristine (Mark) Kothenbeutel, of Cedar Rapids, Iowa, Michael, of Dubuque, Jeff, of Cedar Rapids, and Mark (Teresa), of Red Wing, Minn.; grandchildren, Kaitlyn, Jaclyn, Andre
2 CONC w, Tyler, Timothy and Tanner; a sister, Sara (Don) Moe, of Cedar Falls, Iowa; a niece, Stacy; and a nephew, Tim.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents; and a brother, Donald.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Virginia Lou House (1934 - 2012)*
2 CONT
