1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/155253297/elmond-m-larson
2 CONT
2 CONT Elmond M. Larson, 81, lifelong Argyle and Blanchardville area resident, died Sunday, March 3, 1963, in St. Clare hospital following an extended illness. Elmond Merril Larson (known as Almon) was born in the Town of York, Green Cou
2 CONC nty, June 29, 1881, the son of Lars E. and Caroline Strommen Larson. He worked as a carpenter in the Argyle-Blanchardville area for many years.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by five half-brothers, Thomas and Andrew Erickson, Blanchardville; Edward Erickson, Browntown; Martin Erickson, Gratiot, and Amos Erickson, Argyle. He is preceded in death by his parents, his step-father, Ole Ericks
2 CONC on, and a brother, Anton Larson, on Oct. 28, 1958.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be in the Blanchardville Lutheran church. Rev. Edward Swanson will officiate. Burial will be in Graceland cemetery, Blanchardville. Saether Funeral Home was in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Monroe Evening Times, March 6, 1963 – page 6 (JnJSchober)
