1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/94108682/ole-erickson
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Erickson, for thirty-five years a farmer in Green county, passed away on February 2nd, at the age of sixty-eight years, nine months and twenty-nine days. He had been ill since last July. Funeral services were held at the late 
2 CONC home in Moscow and at the Lutheran church in the village Thursday afternoon, February 5th, at one o’clock, Rev. J.A. Houkom officiating. The choir of the Lutheran church sang. The remains were interred at Graceland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Erickson Lovskogen was born in S. Aurdal, Valers, Norway, April 3rd, 1856. In 1884 he came to America and took up life in his accepted country as a farmer in York Township. His marriage to Caroline Strommen occurred on Decembe
2 CONC r 13, 1887. Five sons were born to this union, namely: Eddie of Yellowstone, Martin, Thomas, Amos and Andrew. York Township continued to be their home until in 1919, when they retired from farming and came to this village, since w
2 CONC hich time Mr. Erickson worked as a day laborer until he became ill. He was a member of Blanchardville Lutheran church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides his wife and the five sons above mentioned, the deceased is survived by two step-sons, Anton and Elmond Larson; and two aged brothers, Andrew and Syver Erickson, both of York Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Erickson was known as an honest, hardworking man, of sterling worth and very cheerful disposition.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source Blanchardville Blade, Feb 12, 1925 - page 1
