1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/94108684/thomas-o-erickson
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas O. Erickson, 82, a resident of Lafayette Manor Nursing Home in Darlington, formerly of Blanchardville, passed away Sunday morning, Aug. 31, 1980, after a long illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in the Town of York, Green County, on March 30, 1898, the son of Ole and Caroline (Lena) Strommen Erickson. He attended the Loyalty School.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married March 12, 1925, in Freeport, to Mabel Kolden. They farmed in the Blanchardville area until 1966 when they moved to Blanchardville where he did electrical work. His wife passed away in 1972.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include two brothers, Andy of Monticello and Edward of the Lafayette Manor in Darlington, and nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, four brothers, and his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Blanchardville Lutheran Church where services were held Wednesday, Sept. 3, with the Rev. Wayne Henderson officiating. Burial was in Graceland Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Saether Funeral Home in Blanchardville was in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Blade-Atlas, Sept. 4, 1980-page 12 (JnJSchober)
