1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Foreldre, fødselsdato, dåpsdato og dåpsnavn /
2 CONT Parents, date of birth, date of baptism and given names:'''
2 CONT [https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/8969/43799/47 Gran prestekontor, SAH/PREST-112Ministerialbok nr. 12, 1856-1874, s. 890, No: 33]
2 CONT
2 CONT To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/117786159/marie_olson
2 CONT
2 CONT Mari Torstendsdatter was born March 27, 1840 on Lunder farm, Gran, Oppland, Norway, the daughter of Torsten Olsen & Kari Iversdatter. She married Frederick Olsen in 1864 in Gran. They had 3 children in Norway:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Caroline Dortha Fredricksdatter, born September 10, 1864 on Kitelsrud farm, Gran, Oppland, Norway.
2 CONT 2) Oluf Fredricksen, born May 13, 1866 on Heier farm, Gran, Oppland, Norway.
2 CONT 3) Thorvald Fredricksen, born January 10, 1868 on Heier farm, Gran, Oppland, Norway.
2 CONT (above per the Norwegian Digital Archives).
2 CONT
2 CONT Per the Grand Forks County Heritage Book, Fredrick and Maria Olson, came with their children Caroline, Oluf and Thorvald, to the United States and first came to Detroit, Michigan, and later moved to Decorah, Iowa. In 1879, the fam
2 CONC ily moved to North Dakota and settled west of Northwood near the Goose River.
