3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 DEC 1875
2 ADDR
3 CITY York
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 AUG 1953
2 ADDR
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=94108655
2 CONT
2 CONT Carrie Lageson Emberson was born in the town of York on Dec. 6, 1875, of the parents Engebret and Anna Benson Lageson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since her marriage to Anton Emberson in 1896 she has resided on the same farm up to her death. She attended the Swiggum rural school. She passed away at her farm home on Friday, August 21, 1953, at the age of 70 years, 8 months an
2 CONC d 15 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of the Blanchardville Lutheran church and Ladies Aid Society.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two daughters, Mrs. Ben (Alma) Hermanson and Mrs. Sherman (Clara) Hermanson of Blanchardville; five sons, Arthur of Argyle, Glenn, Ben, Willard and Everett of Blanchardville; two brothers, Anton and Ed Lageson of Bla
2 CONC nchardville; 13 grandchildren, and four great-grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband and two sons, three sisters and one brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted by Rev. T. Kleven at the Blanchardville Lutheran church Monday afternoon at 1:30 with burial in Graceland cemetery. Pallbearers were Bennet Moen, Edwin H. Hanson, Donald Lageson, Glen Lageson, Marti
2 CONC n Norton and Wilmer Emberson. In memoriam gifts totaled $171.00.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Blanchardville Blade, Aug 27, 1953 (Contributor JnJSchober) 
2 CONT
