1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=94108853
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Bennie Hermanson, 58, a lifelong resident of the area, died on Monday night at a Madison hospital following a long illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be held at 1:30 p.m. Friday in the Blanchardville Lutheran church, Rev. Torgerson officiating. Interment will be in Graceland cemetery. Friends may call at the Saether funeral home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Hermanson was the former Alma Karen Emberson, daughter of Anton and Carrie Lageson Emberson. She was born June 29, 1897, in the Town of Blanchard and attended Blanchardville schools. Her marriage to Bennie Hermanson occurred 
2 CONC Feb. 16, 1922, at the Blanchardville Lutheran parsonage. She was a member of the Lutheran church.
2 CONT
2 CONT She leaves her husband; three daughters, Mrs. Ken Poulsen and Mrs. Lyle Johnson, both of Madison, and Mrs. Lloyd Junge of Morrisonville; a son, Otis, Monticello; a sister, Mrs. Sherman Hermanson, Blanchardville; five brothers, Art
2 CONC hur Emberson, Argyle, and Willard, Everett, Glen and Bennie, Blanchardville; four grandchildren, and a nephew, Richard Hermanson, who made his home with her. Two brothers preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Blanchardville Blade, 1955 (Contributor JnJSchober) 
