1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=94108654
2 CONT
2 CONT Bennie M. Emberson, 74, a resident of the Norder Care Home, Argyle, formerly of Blanchardville, died early Tuesday morning, Feb. 15, 1983, at the VA Hospital in Madison. He had been a patient at the hospital since Jan. 4, 1983.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born June 9, 1908, in Blanchard Township, Lafayette County, he was the son of Anton and Carrie Lageson Emberson. He attended schools in the Blanchardville area.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had farmed on the home farm in the Blanchardville area until his retirement. He never married.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include four brothers, Arthur Emberson, Monroe; Willard at the Mineral Point Care Center; Glenn, Argyle and Everette, Madison; and one sister, Mrs. Sherman (Clara) Hermanson, Blanchardville.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents, two brothers and one sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Emberson was a veteran of WWII, having served in the Medical Corp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 11:00 a.m., Friday, Feb 18, in the Blanchardville Lutheran Church of which he was a member. The Rev. Wayne Henderson will officiate. Burial will be in Graceland Cemetery, Blanchardville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held at the Saether Funeral Home, Blanchardville, from 4-9 p.m. on Thursday, February 17.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Blade-Atlas, Feb. 17, 1983-page 12 (Contributor JnJSchober) 
