2 CONT
2 CONT Willard John Emberson, 77, Mineral Point and formerly of Blanchardville, died Saturday, July 23, 1988 at the Mineral Point Living Center. Born on June 28, 1911 in Blanchardville, he was the son of Anton and Carrie (Lageson) Embers
2 CONC on. He attended school in Blanchardville. He farmed on the home farm with his brother, Everette, until retiring to Blanchardville. For the past 10 years he has lived in Mineral Point. He was a member of the Blanchardville Lutheran
2 CONC  Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by three brothers, Arthur of Monroe, Glenn of Argyle and Everette of Madison; and a sister, Mrs. Sherman (Clara) Hermanson of Blanchardville.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents; three brothers, Bennie, Marion and Henry; and a sister, Alma Hermanson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Tuesday, July 26 at the Blanchardville Lutheran Church with the Rev. Wayne Henderson officiating. Burial was in Graceland Cemetery, Blanchardville. The Saether Funeral Home, Blanchardville, was in charge
2 CONC  of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Blade-Atlas, July 28, 1988 – page 8 (Contributor JnJSchober) 
