2 CONT OBITUARY: Everette Martin Emberson, 83, Madison, formerly of Blanchardville, died Tuesday evening, September 5, 2000 at the Don and Marilyn Anderson HospiceCare Center in Madison. He was born in Blanchardville on the family farm F
2 CONC ebruary 6, 1917 to Anton and Carrie (Lageson) Emberson. He attended school in Blanchardville. He was married on October 31, 1955 in the Bethel Lutheran Church in Madison to Rosalie June Winters. Everette farmed in Blanchardville f
2 CONC or many years, and then moved to Madison in 1963 where he worked for the University of Wisconsin Heating Plant in Madison. He retired from there in 1965. He was a member of the Blanchardville Lutheran Church, where he was baptized
2 CONC  and confirmed. He loved hunting, fishing and spending time with his grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his wife, Rosalie, Madison; one son, Eddie (Debbie) Emberson, Madison; three grandchildren, Aaron Emberson of Florida and Stacy and Sean Emberson, both of Madison; and many nieces, nephews and dear friends and fa
2 CONC mily. He is preceded in death by his parents; one son, Dennis, who died May 31, 1998; and six brothers and two sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT A funeral service was held Friday, September 8 at 11 a.m. at the Blanchardville Lutheran Church in Blanchardville. Rev. Tom Boll and Rev. Mark Gruner of the Pecatonica Lutheran Parish officiated with burial in Graceland Cemetery, 
2 CONC Blanchardville. Friends called Thursday evening, September 9 from 4-9 p.m. at the Saether Funeral Home in Blanchardville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Pecatonica Valley Leader, Sept 14, 2000 – page 16 (Contributor JnJSchober) 
