2 CONT OBITUARY: Clara Hermanson, 90, of The Monroe manor, formerly of Blanchardville, died Sunday, January 8, 1995 in The Monroe Manor. She was born January 14, 1904 in York Township, the son of Anton and Carrie (Lageson) Emberson. She 
2 CONC attended Blanchardville area rural school and graduated from Blanchardville High School in 1922 and Platteville Teachers College in 1923. She married Sherman Hermanson on August 22, 1925 in Blanchardville Lutheran Parsonage. She t
2 CONC aught in various Blanchardville area rural schools including Loyalty and Puddledock schools until she devoted full time to farming with her husband Sherman and her family. She enjoyed playing the piano, quilting and gardening. She
2 CONC  was a member of the Blanchardville Lutheran Church, Women of the ELCA and the Esther Circle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her husband, Sherman of The Monroe Manor, formerly of Blanchardville; one son, David (Ursula) Hermanson, Blanchardville; one brother, Everette (Rosalie) Emberson, Madison; three grandchildren, Steven (Kelly) Herm
2 CONC anson and Christina Hermanson, both of Blanchardville and Pamela (Kelly) Rushmen, Mequon; two great-grandchildren and two step-great-grandchildren. She was preceded in death by her parents; six brothers, Marion, Willard, Bennie, H
2 CONC enry, Arthur and Glenn; and one sister, Alma Hermanson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Wednesday, January 11 at the Blanchardville Lutheran Church in Blanchardville. Rev. Jeff Miller of the Pecatonica Lutheran Parish officiated with burial in Graceland Cemetery, Blanchardville. The Saether
2 CONC  Funeral Home, Blanchardville, was in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Blade-Atlas, Jan 12, 1995 – page 8 (Contributor JnJSchober) 
