1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ernest, 98, passed away Saturday in Norman, OK. He was born in Cement, OK to Otto and Minnie (Dryden) Dahl. In 1932 Ernest graduated from high school in Houston, TX. Shortly after graduating he went to work in the 
2 CONC oil fields. In 1937 he married the love of his life, Angie Ferguson and together they shared over 50 years together. In 1942 Ernest was drafted by the U.S. Army and proudly served his country as a Combat Engineer. He re-enlisted i
2 CONC n 1945 and went on to serve with the Army Signal Corps CeeBee's division. Upon his return, Ernest worked for Fain-Porter Drilling of OKC for 47 years and consulted for many years after that. He and his wife were members at Crossro
2 CONC ads Cathedral for many years where they were both very involved. He was an elder and usher at the church and also helped with many church projects including constructing sets for the Easter Pageants and other productions. Aside fr
2 CONC om the church, family was very important to Ernest. He was a loving husband, father, grandfather and wonderful friend. He will be missed by everyone in his life. 
