1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=24317942
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Brede "Brady" O. Grina passed away at age 72 on Wednesday, October 21, 1936 in Northwood. He had been poorly and failing since a stroke he suffered in 1933. Deceased was chief engineer of the Northwood Fire Dept for 26 years, sinc
2 CONC e 1910. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Grina was born on Juy 4, 1864 not far from Clermont, Iowa. He came to Pelican Rapids, MN with his parents, when just a small boy, and came to the Northwood community in 1882, at 18 years of age. He stayed for a short time with
2 CONC  his brother, Peter Grina, a farmer residing near Northwood. He had a wood yard and feed mill in town here for several years, was janitor of the Northwood Public Schools for several years, and worked for some years at the Slawson 
2 CONC Merchantile Co. store. He also ran a confectionery store for a period of years, and was employed at the Municipal Light and Power Plant of Northwood from 1925 until incapacited by a stroke on Sept. 23, 1933. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held from the United Lutheran Church on Monday, October 26, 1936. Interment was at the Northwood Cemetery. Mr. Grina married Lena Tangen in 1888, who survives him. He has 7 surviving children: Peter Oscar, Me
2 CONC lvin, Hilda, Victor, Linton, Birdie, and Eunice. He is also survived by three brothers, Ed Grina of Heimdal, ND, Iver Grina of Barnesville, MN, and Melvin Grina of McGregor, ND. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was a good husband and a kindly father, devoted to his home, and during all the years of active citizenship, displayed a fidelity to duty and faithfulness to every office of public trust, that marked him a man of hono
2 CONC r and high integrity. The years cannot dime the memory of his service to his fellow-men, nor the many virtues that made him an outstanding citizen. He was a good engineer, and served both the Northwood Fire Department and the City
2 CONC  of Northwood, most faithfully and well. May we believe, that for him now comes blessed rest and tranquility and peace and joy in the realms of the immortals, forever more.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/24317942/brede-o_-grina]
